# npm-advisor-mcp — example environment variables.
#
# The server itself does NOT load a .env file at startup. Copy the values
# below into:
#
#   - The "env" block of your MCP client config
#     (claude_desktop_config.json, .vscode/mcp.json, .cursor/mcp.json, etc.)
#     — recommended; the client passes them to the spawned subprocess.
#
#   - OR your shell, before running the binary directly:
#       cp .env.example .env && set -a && source .env && set +a
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you need.

# GitHub personal-access token. Lifts the GitHub REST API limit from
# 60 req/hr (unauthenticated, per IP) to 5,000 req/hr (per token).
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens — only "public_repo"
# read scope is required; the server never touches private repositories.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Bearer token required by the HTTP transport (--http) when bound to a
# non-loopback host. Choose a long random string; clients must send
# `Authorization: Bearer <this value>` on every request. Leave unset
# for stdio mode or for loopback-only HTTP.
# MCP_HTTP_TOKEN=
